% Test cases for the intrapulmonary percussive ventilation policy (ipv.le):
% synthetic claims for E0481, which LCD L33786 denies whatever the record
% shows. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query, so
% "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary, and
% what minimal change would make it payable — none, for an E0481 claim.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base ipv cases includes these resources:
    ipv.

the knowledge base ipv cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month claim: every documentation requirement of dmepos.le
% in the record, the beneficiary at home. Not reasonable and necessary, not
% payable, and no change to the record makes it payable.
scenario complete_record is:
    claim 1 is for the IPV system.
    the HCPCS code of the IPV system is "E0481".
    the IPV system is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the order for the IPV system is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the IPV system is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the IPV system includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the IPV system includes order date.
    the order for the IPV system includes description of the item.
    the order for the IPV system includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the IPV system includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the IPV system was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the IPV system was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the IPV system.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].
    flip expects changes [].

% A purchase rather than a rental, with the same record: the same denial.
scenario purchase is:
    claim 1 is for the IPV system.
    the HCPCS code of the IPV system is "E0481".
    the IPV system is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% The fourth rental month with continued need and use documented: the
% denial does not depend on the month.
scenario rental_month_4 is:
    claim 1 is for the IPV system.
    the HCPCS code of the IPV system is "E0481".
    the IPV system is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    the medical record documents continued need for the IPV system on 2026-05-15.
    the record documents continued use of the IPV system on 2026-05-15.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% The system furnished in a hospital: the item is not within the benefit
% (durable medical equipment is used in the home), so the claim fails
% earlier, at applicability.
scenario hospital_residence is:
    claim 1 is for the IPV system.
    the HCPCS code of the IPV system is "E0481".
    the IPV system is furnished to Dee.
    the residence of Dee is hospital.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% A claim for a high frequency chest wall oscillation device (E0483): not a
% code of this policy, so outside the scope of this program.
scenario other_code is:
    claim 1 is for the vest system.
    the HCPCS code of the vest system is "E0483".
    the vest system is furnished to Eve.
    the residence of Eve is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].
